  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kvinna till Kvinna Rwanda 2021-2024 - KtK phase II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna Rwanda 2021-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal is to strengthen the capacity and coordination of the women&apos;s movement in Rwanda for more strategic interventions to enhance women&apos;s voice and participation, freedom from violence and full enjoyment of human rights.

&#xa0;This goal is aimed to be achieved through the following pathways:

Objective 1: Partners organisations are stronger, more effective and 
work more strategically and collaboratively

Objective 2: Improved protection from gender based violence with a 
specific focus on prevention

Objective 3: Rights holders and duty bearers have an increased 
understanding and respect for Sexual and Reproductive Health and 
Rights (SRHR)

Objective 4: Enhanced qualitative participation of women in decision 
making and conflict resolution.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r insatsen &#xe4;r att bidra till att st&#xe4;rka kvinnor&#xf6;relsens kapacitet i Rwanda f&#xf6;r mer strategiskt arbete f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kvinnors r&#xf6;st och deltagande, frihet fr&#xe5;n v&#xe5;ld och fulla &#xe5;tnjutande av m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter.

Kvinna till Kvinna har verkat i Rwanda sedan 2017, d&#xe5; ambassaden beslutade att finansiera Kvinna till Kvinnas f&#xf6;rsta landprogram i Rwanda. Programmets &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l har varit att bidra till en starkare och mer samverkande kvinnor&#xe4;ttighetsr&#xf6;relse i Rwanda samt att arbeta mer effektivt f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och kvinnors egenmakt. Det nya programf&#xf6;rslaget f&#xf6;r 2021 - 2024 bygger p&#xe5; framg&#xe5;ngar, utmaningar och l&#xe4;rdomar fr&#xe5;n den nuvarande fasen, samtidigt som fokus flyttas f&#xf6;r att svara p&#xe5; socioekonomisk och politisk utveckling f&#xf6;r att b&#xe4;ttre svara p&#xe5; kvinnors och flickors behov. Insatsen &#xe4;r strukturerat som ett programst&#xf6;d med tv&#xe5; delar. I den f&#xf6;rsta delen vidarebefordras medel till partnerorganisationer f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra sina egna aktiviteter. I den andra delen genomf&#xf6;r Kvinna till Kvinna aktiviteter f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka deras partners totala kapacitet som kvinnor&#xe4;ttighetsorganisationer och f&#xf6;r att h&#xf6;ja deras f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att samordna och driva den nationella dialogen.

Programmet delas in i fyra huvudm&#xe5;l:

- Partners &#xe4;r starkare, effektivare och arbetar mer strategiskt och samarbete
- F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrat skydd mot k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld med s&#xe4;rskilt fokus p&#xe5; f&#xf6;rebyggande
- R&#xe4;ttighetsinnehavare och ansvarsb&#xe4;rare (duty bearers) har &#xf6;kad f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else och respekt f&#xf6;r sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter (SRHR)
- F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrat kvalitativt deltagande av kvinnor i beslutsfattande och konfliktl&#xf6;sning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of the intervention is to contribute to strengthen the capacity and coordination of the women&#x2019;s movement in Rwanda for more strategic interventions to enhance women&#x2019;s voice and participation, freedom from violence and full enjoyment of human rights.

Kvinna till Kvinna has operated in Rwanda since 2017, when the Embassy decided to fund Kvinna till Kvinna&#x2019;s first country programme in Rwanda. The overall aim of the programme has been to contribute towards a stronger and more connected women&#x2019;s rights movement in Rwanda, working more effectively for gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment.  The new Kvinna till Kvinna&#x2019;s proposal for 2021 &#x2013; 2024 builds on the successes, challenges and lessons learned under the current phase while at the same time shifting the focus of the program to respond to socio-economic and political developments and emerging priorities to better respond to the needs of women and girls. The contribution is structured as a programme support with two pillars. The first pillar, which represents the majority of the programmes funding, is forwarded to partner organizations to implement their own activities. In the second pillar, Kvinna till Kvinna itself implement activities to increase their partners overall capacity as women&#x2019;s rights organizations as well as their capacity to coordinate and pursue advocacy and national dialogue.

The key impact objectives are:
- Partners are stronger, more effective and work more strategically
- Improved protection from gender-based violence with a specific focus on prevention
- Rights holders and duty bearers have an increased understanding and respect for Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR)
- Enhanced qualitative participation of women in decision making and conflict resolution.</narrative>
  </description>
